.TH LFS-LINUX 1 "September 2026" "lfs-linux 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lfs-linux \- verify, install, and launch Live for Speed in a private Wine prefix
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lfs-linux
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lfs-linux
is an unofficial open-source launcher for the untouched official Live for Speed Windows build.
It verifies downloaded LFS, Wine, and DXVK payloads, authenticates the Wine package with its detached Arch packager signature, and keeps game and player files in user-owned XDG directories.
After first installation, LFS owns game files and updates. The wrapper verifies compatibility components, not installed game fingerprints.
Live for Speed 0.8C20 is a public test and is not represented as stable.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Run interactive first-use setup.
.TP
.B install
Download, verify, and install or repair pinned upstream runtime files.
.TP
.B launch
Check compatibility components and start LFS without an installed-game fingerprint gate.
.TP
.B recover-update
Legacy compatibility notice. Updates no longer require wrapper recovery; launch normally.
.TP
.B stop
Request a clean game exit, then stop only the private Wine prefix if needed.
.TP
.B doctor
Report host, runtime, manifest, and installation checks.
.TP
.B status
Show bootstrap pins, installation presence, paths, and process state. Check the game version inside LFS.
.TP
.B update-check
Compare release pins with the official LFS downloads page without modifying LFS.
.TP
.B verify-sources
Download and verify all pinned release inputs.
.TP
.B ready
Return success only when the installation is valid and ready to launch.
.TP
.B remove
Remove the user installation after explicit confirmation.
.TP
.B purge-cache
Remove wrapper downloads and shader caches.
.TP
.B help
Show command help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/lfs-linux
Private Wine runtime, prefix, game files, and any retained legacy update records.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/lfs-linux
Verified downloads and disposable caches.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/lfs-linux
Launcher and DXVK logs.
.SH SAFETY
Do not run game installation or launch commands as root.
Normal system-package removal does not delete user profiles, settings, replays, mods, game files, caches, or local update baselines.
The wrapper and distribution package do not contain proprietary game payloads.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation: https://github.com/mitzracing/live-for-speed-linux

.SH GRAPHICAL USE
Open Live for Speed Linux from the application menu for graphical installation,
progress, compatibility-component repair, and automatic launch.
Accept updates inside LFS and reopen normally after closing. No wrapper update approval is needed.
The desktop helper accepts launch, setup, doctor, help, and recover-update.
A branded GTK window replaces the first-run terminal. Download progress uses
measured bytes. Other steps use an indeterminate indicator. Help previews a small
diagnostic report before the player saves it or opens the support website.
.PP
The default selects GTK when available, with Zenity as the initial fallback.
Set LFS_LINUX_UI=zenity to select Zenity, or LFS_LINUX_UI=gtk to require GTK.
The controller does not switch views after an operation starts.
